{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Encounter.MostowRigidity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Encounter.MostowRigidity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.Knot.Clausen","lean:module:QOU.Knot.ClausenValueBounds","lean:module:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoVolumeChord","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.BlochWignerPositive"],"declarations":21,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Encounter.MostowRigidity.mass_eigenvalue_isolated","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Encounter.MostowRigidity.mass_eigenvalue_isolated","kind":"theorem","line":354,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Encounter/MostowRigidity.lean#L354-L369","doc":"**Downstream consumer: mass eigenvalue is isolated**.\n\nGeneric theorem in the §3b conditional-class consumer\npattern: takes `[MostowRigidity M]` as a typeclass hypothesis\nand concludes that the mass eigenvalue attached to `M` is\nisolated by a strictly positive Mostow gap.\n\nAny new instance of `MostowRigidity` automatically validates\nthis theorem without rewriting the proof — that is the\noperational pay-off of the §3b conditional-class pattern.\nThree closed inhabitants exist in this module\n(`Unknot`, `FigureEight`, `Knot5_2`); each immediately\ndischarges the hypothesis and yields a closed conclusion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Encounter.MostowRigidity.figureEight_volume_lt_knot5_2_volume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Encounter.MostowRigidity.figureEight_volume_lt_knot5_2_volume","kind":"theorem","line":332,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Encounter/MostowRigidity.lean#L332-L352","doc":"**Volume comparison: figure-eight < 5_2**.\n\nAdds the second comparison in the hyperbolic-volume spectrum\npopulated by this module.  Together with\n`unknot_volume_lt_figureEight_volume` it exhibits the\nmonotone chain\n\n`volumeInvariant Unknot < volumeInvariant FigureEight\n   < volumeInvariant Knot5_2`\n\nand demonstrates that the class supports genuine spectral\nbookkeeping rather than a single anchored comparison. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Encounter.MostowRigidity.knot5_2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Encounter.MostowRigidity.knot5_2","kind":"instance","line":272,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Encounter/MostowRigidity.lean#L272-L330","doc":"**Concrete instance: 5_2 knot complement**.\n\nThe complement `S^3 \\ 5_2` is the second-smallest known\norientable cusped hyperbolic 3-manifold (after `S^3 \\ 4_1`),\nwith hyperbolic volume\n\n`Vol(5_2) ≈ 2.82812208833078`\n\n(SnapPy ManifoldHP 50 dps, 2026-06-12; witness field\n`vol_5_2_decimal_50`. The former Adams-Hildebrand-Weeks 1991\n15-dps anchor `2.82812208833410` carried a digit-13–15\ntranscription error.)\n\nThe Mostow gap is bounded below by `0.3`.\n\n**This was `0.5`, and `0.5` is not a lower bound.**  The field is documented as a\n*lower bound* on the distance to the next distinct spectrum value, and the next value\nabove `Vol(5_2)` is `Vol(6_1) ≈ 3.16396`, i.e. a gap of `0.33584`.  The old docstring\ncalled `0.5` \"well under the nearest-neighbour gaps ... `Vol(6_1) - Vol(5_2) ≈ 0.336`\"\nwhile quoting that very figure — `0.5 > 0.336`, so the value contradicted the sentence\nthat justified it.  `figureEight`'s `0.5` is sound by contrast: its neighbour up is\n`Vol(5_2)`, a gap of `0.798`.\n\nNothing in Lean broke, because the class carries only `mostow_gap_pos` and explicitly\ndefers the discreteness claim to Mathlib's geometric-topology layer (see the class\ndocstring).  That is exactly why it went unnoticed: the field's *documented* meaning is\nnot enforced by its *stated* obligation, so an agent trusting the doc would conclude no\nhyperbolic volume lies within `0.5` of `Vol(5_2)`, and `Vol(6_1)` does.\n\nRef: Adams, Hildebrand, Weeks, *Hyperbolic invariants of\nknots and links*, Trans. AMS 326 (1991) 1–56. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Encounter.MostowRigidity.unknot_volume_lt_figureEight_volume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Encounter.MostowRigidity.unknot_volume_lt_figureEight_volume","kind":"theorem","line":254,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Encounter/MostowRigidity.lean#L254-L270","doc":"**Volume comparison: unknot < figure-eight**.\n\nSanity check: the volume invariant attached to the\n`unknot` instance (`0`, by Thurston's convention) is\nstrictly smaller than the volume invariant attached to the\n`figureEight` instance (`Vol(4_1) ≈ 2.02988`).  This is the\nsmallest non-trivial volume comparison in the\nhyperbolic-volume spectrum and the first non-degenerate\nuse of `volumeInvariant`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Encounter.MostowRigidity.figureEight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Encounter.MostowRigidity.figureEight","kind":"instance","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Encounter/MostowRigidity.lean#L210-L252","doc":"**Concrete instance: figure-eight knot complement** (`4_1`).\n\nThe complement `S^3 \\ 4_1` is the smallest known orientable\ncusped hyperbolic 3-manifold (Cao–Meyerhoff 2001), with\nhyperbolic volume\n\n`Vol(4_1) = 2 · Cl₂(π/3) = 6 · Λ(π/3) ≈ 2.02988...`\n\nwhere `Cl₂` is the Clausen function and `Λ` the Lobachevsky\nfunction, `Λ(θ) = Cl₂(2θ)/2`.  The class field\nstores the 15-significant-digit truncation\n`2.02988321281930` (kept in lock-step with the canonical\n50-dps witness via `:leanval[Vol_4_1]{precision=15}`); the\ndirection of the truncation does not affect the class\ninvariants.\n\nThe Mostow gap is bounded below by `0.5`, a conservative\nunder-approximation of the next-smallest gap\n\n`Vol(5_2) - Vol(4_1) ≈ 2.82812 - 2.02988 ≈ 0.798`.\n\nRef: [thurston1978]; Cao–Meyerhoff, *The orientable cusped\nhyperbolic 3-manifolds of minimum volume*, Invent. Math. 146\n(2001) 451–478. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Encounter.MostowRigidity.unknot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Encounter.MostowRigidity.unknot","kind":"instance","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Encounter/MostowRigidity.lean#L190-L208","doc":"**Concrete instance: unknot complement** (degenerate\nhyperbolic case).\n\nBy Thurston's extension of `Vol` to the whole knot-complement\nspectrum, non-hyperbolic complements are assigned volume 0.\nThe unknot complement is the solid torus, which is\nSeifert-fibred and not hyperbolic; its conventional volume is\ntherefore 0.  The Mostow gap is bounded below by `1` —\na conservative under-approximation of\n`Vol(4_1) ≈ 2.0299`, the smallest known hyperbolic\n3-manifold volume (Cao–Meyerhoff 2001).\n\nRef: [thurston1978] §6 (volume of non-hyperbolic complements\nby convention) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Encounter.MostowRigidity.Knot5_2.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Encounter.MostowRigidity.Knot5_2.mk","kind":"ctor","line":188,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Encounter/MostowRigidity.lean#L188-L188","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Encounter.MostowRigidity.Knot5_2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Encounter.MostowRigidity.Knot5_2","kind":"structure","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Encounter/MostowRigidity.lean#L187-L188","doc":"Type marker for the 5_2 knot complement. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Encounter.MostowRigidity.FigureEight.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Encounter.MostowRigidity.FigureEight.mk","kind":"ctor","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Encounter/MostowRigidity.lean#L185-L185","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Encounter.MostowRigidity.FigureEight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Encounter.MostowRigidity.FigureEight","kind":"structure","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Encounter/MostowRigidity.lean#L184-L185","doc":"Type marker for the figure-eight knot complement `4_1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Encounter.MostowRigidity.Unknot.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Encounter.MostowRigidity.Unknot.mk","kind":"ctor","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Encounter/MostowRigidity.lean#L182-L182","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Encounter.MostowRigidity.Unknot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Encounter.MostowRigidity.Unknot","kind":"structure","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Encounter/MostowRigidity.lean#L180-L182","doc":"Type marker for the unknot complement (used as the carrier of\nthe corresponding `MostowRigidity` instance). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Encounter.MostowRigidity.volumeInvariant_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Encounter.MostowRigidity.volumeInvariant_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Encounter/MostowRigidity.lean#L176-L178","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Encounter.MostowRigidity.volumeInvariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Encounter.MostowRigidity.volumeInvariant","kind":"def","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Encounter/MostowRigidity.lean#L169-L174","doc":"**Volume of the categorical mass eigenvalue** — extraction\nhelper.  Returns the underlying volume invariant from the\n`MostowRigidity` class so that downstream uses can quote\n`volumeInvariant M` rather than `(inferInstance : MostowRigidity M).volume`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Encounter.MostowRigidity.mass_rigidity_of_mostow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Encounter.MostowRigidity.mass_rigidity_of_mostow","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Encounter/MostowRigidity.lean#L140-L167","doc":"**Mass rigidity from Mostow** — fully-proved downstream\nconditional theorem.\n\nGiven `[MostowRigidity M]` for the knot complement `M`, the\ncategorical mass eigenvalue (which factors through the\nhyperbolic volume via the `algebraic-quantum-volume` bridge)\nis well-defined (non-negative volume) and **isolated**: the\nnext distinct value in the volume spectrum lies strictly above\n`volume`, separated by the Mostow gap.\n\nBoth conjuncts are *derived*, not projected: the first is the\nnon-negativity witness, and the second — `volume` is strictly\nbelow its gap-separated successor `volume + mostow_gap` — is\nderived from the strict positivity of the gap\n(`lt_add_of_pos_right`).  Composing the two fields rather than\nre-exporting `mostow_gap_pos` verbatim is what makes this a\ngenuine rigidity consequence (separation of the eigenvalue from\nthe rest of the spectrum) rather than a self-assuming\nprojection (AGENTS.md §3b-cond item 5).\n\nThis is the §3b-cond rigorous-conditional companion to the\n`prop:mostow-confinement` content block; concrete instances\nof the class supply the rigidity proof for specific knot\ncomplements. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Encounter.MostowRigidity.MostowRigidity.mostow_gap_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Encounter.MostowRigidity.MostowRigidity.mostow_gap_pos","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Encounter/MostowRigidity.lean#L138-L138","doc":"The Mostow gap is strictly positive.  This is the\noperational content of \"no nearby hyperbolic structures\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Encounter.MostowRigidity.MostowRigidity.mostow_gap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Encounter.MostowRigidity.MostowRigidity.mostow_gap","kind":"def","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Encounter/MostowRigidity.lean#L135-L135","doc":"Strictly positive lower bound on the distance from `volume`\nto the next distinct value in the hyperbolic-volume spectrum.\nEncodes Mostow's discreteness witness. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Encounter.MostowRigidity.MostowRigidity.volume_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Encounter.MostowRigidity.MostowRigidity.volume_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Encounter/MostowRigidity.lean#L131-L131","doc":"Volume is non-negative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Encounter.MostowRigidity.MostowRigidity.volume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Encounter.MostowRigidity.MostowRigidity.volume","kind":"def","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Encounter/MostowRigidity.lean#L129-L129","doc":"Hyperbolic volume invariant of `M`.  Convention: take\n`volume = 0` for non-hyperbolic complements. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Encounter.MostowRigidity.MostowRigidity.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Encounter.MostowRigidity.MostowRigidity.mk","kind":"ctor","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Encounter/MostowRigidity.lean#L126-L126","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Encounter.MostowRigidity.MostowRigidity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Encounter.MostowRigidity.MostowRigidity","kind":"class","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Encounter/MostowRigidity.lean#L110-L138","doc":"**Mostow rigidity (conditional class)**.\n\nA `MostowRigidity M` instance attaches to `M` a hyperbolic\nvolume invariant `volume` together with a strictly positive\nMostow gap `mostow_gap` to the next distinct value in the\nvolume spectrum.\n\nOperationally this is what downstream theorems consume:\nrigidity of the volume (its bare existence as a class field)\nplus discreteness of the spectrum (the strictly positive\ngap).  Concrete instances must supply both reals and both\npositivity witnesses; the §3b \"hard work\" of *proving* that\n`mostow_gap` matches the actual gap to the next hyperbolic\nvolume is deferred to Mathlib's geometric-topology layer.\n\nRef: [mostow1968] ","signatureChunk":0}]}